   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blak_and_Blu",
   "resumo_en": "Blak and Blu is the major-label debut studio album by American musician Gary Clark Jr., released on October 22, 2012. The album touches on a wide variety of traditionally black music genres, including soul (\"Please Come Home\"), hip-hop/R&B (\"The Life\"), Chuck Berry-esque rock and roll (\"Travis County\"), and Clark's trademark, blues (\"When My Train Pulls In\", \"Numb\", \"Next Door Neighbor Blues\").\nBlak and Blu netted Clark his first two Grammy Award nominations, one for Best Rock Song (\"Ain't Messin Round\") and the other for Best Traditional R&B Performance (\"Please Come Home\") which won. This marked the first time that an artist was nominated in both categories in the same year. It peaked at number six on the Billboard 200 album chart, and number one on the Blues Albums chart.",
